    <marc:datafield tag="520" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
      <marc:subfield code="a">Young Maya is shy, and she often feels fragile and scared because of her asthma... except for when she&apos;s in the water, the one place where she feels strong. While many in the fishing village are afraid of &quot;the Beast&quot; -- the giant wave heard throughout the town as it crashes -- Maya finds it beautiful and mesmerizing. She dreams of riding the waves like the brave boys she watches from the show. Many doubt that a girl can surf the biggest waves. But with a special surfboard from her dad and a courageous heart, Maya will show everyone that a girl can meet the Beast head-on.</marc:subfield>
    </marc:datafield>
